# Reloading a redefined package in one bluetcl process must show the new
# definition (see stale.tcl).  The two versions are compiled from their own
# directories (bsc writes each .bo beside its source) and the first is put
# in place before the script runs.  The packages are in BH syntax and the
# script runs in BH syntax.
#
# Known bug: the second query shows the struct's member with the first
# version's synonym expansion (Bit 8) next to a width computed from the
# second (20).  A memo keyed on the synonym's name alone survives the
# reload.  The expected output is the correct one; the comparison is
# registered as an expected failure until the type tables are keyed on
# content (doc/engine-first-plan.md, P1 record, leak closure).

compile_pass v1/StaleT.bs
compile_pass v2/StaleT.bs
copy v1/StaleT.bo StaleT.bo
bluetcl_run_bh_compare_pass_bug stale.tcl {} {} {} "stale synonym payload after a package reload"
